<title>SOUTH KOREA: Cheiljedang buys 20,000T U.S. soybeans.</title>
<headline>Cheiljedang buys 20,000T U.S. soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp has bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. No 2 soybeans at basis over November futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, a company official said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The official said the company bought from Marubeni Corp for shipment in early October from the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>The official did not give further details.</p>
<p>Traders said the soybean purchase was made at around $320 to $325 per tonne, FOB.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
